# Line-ending policy.
#
# Everything is stored in the repository with LF. Without this file, a clone on
# a machine with core.autocrlf=true checks the shell suites out with CRLF, and
# bash then fails on the carriage return — the test runner breaks on a fresh
# clone for a reason that has nothing to do with the code.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Scripts that are executed, not just read. These must be LF everywhere.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.php text eol=lf

# Declared explicitly so Git never attempts end-of-line conversion on them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
